  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#47694\", \"PowerToys#47537\"], \"answer\": \"This has been requested before. PowerToys#47694 asks for the Power Display flyout to appear next to its systray icon, following taskbar orientation, instead of the hardcoded bottom-right position. PowerToys#47537 asks for a top-right or alignment option for the Power Display and Quick Access flyouts for users with a top taskbar. A maintainer replied on #47694 that appearing at the bottom right is by design and that the request is a feature request, not a bug. Nothing in those tickets says it has been changed, so there is no setting or fix to apply yet. Add your thumbs-up and your vertical-taskbar scenario to #47694 so the request can be tracked. If your flyout shows up in the middle of the screen instead of the bottom right, check whether a tool that repositions windows is running, such as Windhawk's 'center new windows' mod. That was the cause in #47537.\"}",
